Z||000007||alpha||11-06-2000||12:31 PM||||IOPORT - (www.ioportracing.com) also sells an SCCA cage for the Fiero. They don't have it listed on their page, but if you email them they will tell you about it. Same with Kirk Racing.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://fiero.dhs.org/fiero/sig.jpg">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu">douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Tigger||11-06-2000||12:51 PM||||I don't want to get off the subject but this just hit me...<P>If Monkeyman put a roll cage in his Fiero, would we call them Monkey Bars?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierov8||11-06-2000||04:24 PM||||Hey -- I'm famous - sorta!<P>That's my car in the initial pic.  Not a roll cage, just the bar.  The bar comes from Kirk Racing.  I got mine through Paeco Imports (they are bigger into British/Import car parts).  They just source roll bars/cages from Kirk.<P>Notes/Important Safety Instructions:<P>1.) Mine is not an SCCA legal bar.  A legal bar will have a crossmember that goes right through the area that the ECU/center console box occupies.  To get a bar made like the one shown in the pic, you will have to call them and ask for it.  Got mine a few years ago when it _was_ a SCCA legal bar.  I just got it because it will be legal for autox/time trialing -- just not road racing :-)<P>2.)  They also make a full cage to fit a factory interior.  <P>3.)  Bar and cage are bolt in.<P>4.)  Bar bolts to the firewall.  Not a really good support structure.  You may want to find a way to tie the bar/cage in to the shock towers.  It's what I did.  Car is a little more rigid now.<P>5.)  If you want to paint the bar, you might ask Kirk to NOT paint it after they are done making it.  The paint shop that shot my bar had a he!! of a time finding out that black Krylon makes a terrible base.<P>Other questions?  Ask or email me!<P>-jeff d<BR>fierov8@tensor.com||||reg||6
Z||000010||Zorba||11-06-2000||08:51 PM|||| What did you pay for a bolt-in cage or bar? Either one will work for me. Did you install it yourself?||||reg||1
Z||000011||Wannabe||11-07-2000||09:58 AM||||A cage to fit the factory interior?! How do they get past the dash vents by the door? ||||reg||1
Z||000012||SibERThuG||11-07-2000||10:43 PM||||I e-mailed ioport racing and this is what he had to say...<P>Yes, we have both a roll bar and cage for this car (fiero). Depending upon what you<BR>get will depend on how easy it is to install. The roll cage and race roll<BR>bar will require removal of the center glove box and relocation of the ECU<BR>(if I remember correctly). Your seats will no longer have full aft travel.<BR>You will have to cut through the carpet. There is probably more.<P>Cost starts at $229.95 and goes up depending upon what you want. Email me<BR>when you know what you want and then I will give you a quote.<P>Ken Myers<BR>Visit our web site at <A HREF="http://www.IOPortRacing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.IOPortRacing.com</A> <BR>&lt;http://www.ioportracing.com/&gt;<P>Doesn't sound worth it to me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Robbie<BR>88' Formula||||reg||1
Z||000013||fierov8||11-08-2000||01:39 PM||||Zorba:<P>Don't remember -- think the bar was around $300 or so.  If memory serves, a friend bought the full cage and spent somewhere around $550.<P>I did the install myself.  It's a full bolt-in.  You do have to cut the carpet and make holes in the cardboard/carpet thingie that sits just below the window.  It might go into a car with a full interior -- I would remove the center console just to give me more room (and the seats, of course ;-) .  Oh yeah -- and roll down your windows -- makes things easier, too!<P>The above assumes you want this to go into a car with a full interior.  Racers have it _much_ easier!<P>I also might've lost some seat travel with the bar installed -- but it wasn't must that was lost!<P>Wannabe:  The front legs of the full cage end up just in front of or just to the "inside" of the vents if I remember correctly -- its been a while since we putzed with getting it inside another car (not mine).<P>SibER -- not sure, but I think IOPort <BR>is selling an Autopower bar/cage.<P>I know that Kirk will make a bar to fit a factory interior, if that is what you desire!<P>lateron,<P>-jeff d<BR>Fort Worth, TX<BR>"streetable in Y2K+1"||||reg||1
